1
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:36,000
Girl Power to the Rescue!

2
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:06,000
Barbie and the Three Musketeers is a animation,
family film directed by William Lau.

3
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:36,000
Corinne is a young country girl who heads to Paris to pursue
her big dream – to become a female musketeer!

4
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:06,000
Never could she imagine she would meet three other
girls who secretly share the same dream!

5
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:36,000
Using their special talents, the girls work together as a
team to foil a plot and save the prince.

6
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:06,000
It's all for one and one for all!

7
00:31:30,000 --> 00:31:36,000
Barbie as Corrine (voice), played by Kelly Sheridan.

8
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Philippe (voice), played by Tim Curry.

9
00:40:30,000 --> 00:40:36,000
Viveca (voice), played by Kira Tozer.

10
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Aramina (voice), played by Willow Johnson.

11
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:36,000
Renée (voice), played by Dorla Bell.

12
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
Corinne's Mother / Fancy Dress Girl #1 (voice), played by Nicole Oliver.

13
00:58:30,000 --> 00:58:36,000
Barbie and the Three Musketeers is a 2009 animated fantasy film.

14
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
It was released to DVD on September 15, 2009, and made its
television premiere on Nickelodeon on November 22, 2009.

15
01:07:30,000 --> 01:07:36,000
This film is the sixteenth entry in the Barbie film series.

16
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
It features the voice of Kelly Sheridan as Corinne d'Artagnan (played by Barbie) and
is based on the 1844 novel The Three Musketeers by Alexandre Dumas.

17
01:16:30,000 --> 01:16:36,000
The film explores themes of female friendship, based on toy,
female protagonist, musketeer, 3d animation.
